afk: the reflink backend degrades to a byte copy when the filesystem
cannot clone extents, unless the new StartOptions.require_cow forbids it.

Motivation: task.isolation.mode is a hard PIN under
omp-isolation-pinned-backend, and the afk distro pins `reflink` (a real
frozen tree — overlayfs reads through to the parent's LIVE worktree, so
every capture leaked parent/sibling writes; see
backlog/2026-08-10-overlayfs-capture-leaks-parent-writes.md in afk).
pi-iso's probe() reports reflink available on ANY Linux without testing
the filesystem, so on ext4/tmpfs the pin used to fail every isolated
spawn at the first clone_file (FICLONE -> EOPNOTSUPP -> IsoError::
Unavailable). Degrading WITHIN the reflink backend is not the fallback
the pin forbids: rcopy fallback changes WHICH FILES the snapshot
contains (drops gitignored files); a byte copy changes only how bytes
are stored — file set, freeze and capture semantics are identical.

Layer note: this patch is Rust-only and is applied by nix/omp-natives.nix
(the natives builder). nix/omp-patched.nix consumes the rebuilt
libpi_natives.so and the regenerated index.d.ts (iso_start gains a 4th
`options` parameter) through its preBuild seam; the TS caller ships in
omp-isolation-require-cow.patch.

What must survive a rebase:
- clone_file: on FICLONE failure with EXDEV|EOPNOTSUPP|ENOTTY|EINVAL|
  ENOSYS and require_cow == false, fall through to std::io::copy on the
  ALREADY-OPEN fds (both at offset 0) instead of erroring; any other
  errno, or require_cow == true, keeps the original error path
  (IsoError::unavailable via map_clone_error, dst unlinked).
- preserve_permissions/set_times_nofollow still run after the copy path
  — mode and mtimes must match the clone path.
- pi_iso::StartOptions { require_cow } + IsolationBackend::start_with
  default method (ignores options); only linux_reflink overrides it and
  its start() forwards to start_with with defaults.
- napi: iso_start(kind?, lower, merged, options?) with
  #[napi(object)] IsoStartOptions { require_cow: Option<bool> },
  dispatching through start_with. No new runtime symbol — index.js
  needs no edit. The CHECKED-IN packages/natives/native/index.d.ts is
  patched by hand (the napi dts regeneration step does not run in the
  nix natives build — verified: an unpatched .d.ts survived a full
  omp-natives rebuild), so the 4th `options` parameter must be kept in
  sync manually on rebases.
- Tests in linux_reflink.rs: tree materialisation + frozen-snapshot
  assertion (parent writes after start are invisible), strict-mode
  refusal, and the /dev/shm (tmpfs) fallback test that exercises the
  real EOPNOTSUPP byte-copy path plus strict refusal on any normal
  Linux host. Tests never assert WHICH path ran on ambient filesystems
  — only content equality and error class.

